.TH ZORO-HARDEN 8 "2026" "Zoro Linux 10" "Zoro Linux Manual"

.SH NAME
zoro\-harden \- Zoro Linux security hardening tool

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zoro\-harden
.RI [ \-\-profile= PROFILE ]
.RI [ \-\-check ]
.RI [ \-\-status ]
.RI [ \-\-revert ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zoro-harden
applies security hardening profiles to a Zoro Linux system.
It configures kernel parameters, disables unused services,
hardens SSH, and optionally runs OpenSCAP remediation.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-profile= PROFILE
Apply a hardening profile. Available profiles:
.RS
.TP
.B zoro-default
Zoro Linux default hardening (recommended).
.TP
.B cis-l1
CIS Benchmark Level 1.
.TP
.B cis-l2
CIS Benchmark Level 2.
.TP
.B stig
DISA STIG profile.
.RE

.TP
.B \-\-check
Audit current system against hardening baseline.

.TP
.B \-\-status
Show current hardening status.

.TP
.B \-\-revert
Revert to pre-hardening defaults.

.TP
.B \-\-list\-profiles
List available profiles.

.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would change without applying.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Apply default hardening:
.B zoro-harden --profile=zoro-default

.TP
Check compliance:
.B zoro-harden --check

.TP
Apply CIS Level 2:
.B zoro-harden --profile=cis-l2

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sysctl.d/99-zoro-hardening.conf
Kernel hardening parameters.
.TP
.I /etc/modprobe.d/zoro-blacklist.conf
Blacklisted kernel modules.
.TP
.I /var/lib/zoro-harden/state
Current hardening state.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zoro-linux (7),
.BR sysctl (8),
.BR firewalld (1),
.BR selinux (8),
.BR oscap (8)

